  11. Whenever an order is a final sale, it earns double points.
  12. Whenever a gift card purchase is made, treat it like any other order for points.
  13. Whenever daily revenue is calculated, count only card orders, each as its items after the discount code plus its shipping, with no tax; store-credit orders bring in no revenue.
  14. Whenever the daily average is calculated, divide revenue by the number of card orders and round down to whole rupees, or use 0 if there are no card orders; do not divide by all orders or by counted orders.
  15. Whenever a day has no orders at all, the daily summary shows zero orders, zero revenue and an average of zero, and no alert is raised.
  16. Should a final-sale order that arrives damaged be refunded? -> A) Yes: refund it as damaged goods, with the shipping fee, up to and including day 90 after delivery, and to the card if it was paid by card.
